RAILWAY OBSTACLE DETECTION - ALL-IN-ONE DASHBOARD  (single file)
Raspberry Pi 4 (2 GB) + TF-Luna LiDAR + HC-SR04 + Pi Camera (5 MP) + L298N + DC geared motor

RUN:      python3 railway_dashboard.py          then open  http://<pi-ip>:5000
INSTALL:  sudo apt update
          sudo apt install -y python3-flask python3-opencv python3-numpy python3-serial \
                              python3-gpiozero python3-lgpio python3-picamera2
          sudo raspi-config -> Interface Options -> Serial Port -> login shell: NO, serial hardware: YES -> reboot

WIRING (physical pin numbers of the 40-pin header)
  TF-Luna (UART)   +5V red   -> Pin 2 (5V)        GND black -> Pin 6 (GND)
                   TXD green -> Pin 10 (GPIO15 RXD)   RXD white -> Pin 8 (GPIO14 TXD)   (config pin: leave open)
  HC-SR04          VCC -> Pin 4 (5V)   GND -> Pin 9 (GND)   TRIG -> Pin 16 (GPIO23)
                   ECHO -> 1k ohm -> Pin 18 (GPIO24) -> 2k ohm -> GND   (voltage divider, ECHO is 5 V!)
  L298N            ENA -> Pin 12 (GPIO18)   IN1 -> Pin 11 (GPIO17)   IN2 -> Pin 13 (GPIO27)
                   GND -> Pin 14 (GND) AND battery minus   +12V terminal -> motor battery plus
                   OUT1/OUT2 -> DC geared motor      (remove the ENA jumper; do not feed L298N 5V into the Pi)
  Pi Camera        ribbon cable -> CSI camera port

Everything (folders, web page, sensors, camera, train control, editor, terminal) is created by this file.
"""
